EXT. FLOATING MARKET ABOVE THE CLOUDS - DAWN

A cluster of rope-slung gondolas drifts on a sea of cloud. Lanterns bob. Between two of them, a plank bridge sways in the wind. The sun rises like a coin.

CALLISTA VALE (40s, sky-pirate captain, sheepskin coat, one glove missing) stands braced at a railing with a spyglass. Behind her, ROOK (teen, deckhand, rope-burned palms) coils line.

ROOK
Captain, the Duskmaw is two points off the port bow.

CALLISTA
I see her, Rook.

ROOK
She's turning.

CALLISTA
They always turn at dawn. It's the only time the clouds agree.

She lowers the glass. Rook comes to the rail. Together they watch a black-sailed ship unfurl like a bat through the mist.

ROOK
We could run.

CALLISTA
We could.

ROOK
Will we?

CALLISTA
Rook, have you ever known me to run?

ROOK
Once.

CALLISTA
That wasn't running. That was a tactical re-evaluation.

Rook grins. Callista takes his shoulder and steers him toward the helm. The ropes sing in the wind.

CALLISTA (CONT'D)
Hard to starboard. Let her come close. Then drop the ballast.

ROOK
All of it?

CALLISTA
All of it.

ROOK
Captain, that's the cargo.

CALLISTA
That's the idea.

He swallows. Then runs for the lever, laughing, as the Duskmaw looms.
